## M3 forwarding constraints

Active core: s1. Baseline paths: s3/s4/s5/s6 → s1.

Do **not** use in normal baseline forwarding: s2 alternate uplinks; s1–s2; s3–s4; h6–s6 secondary. Those links stay physically present for controlled experiments/failover.

Baseline must remain deterministic and loop-free. Do **not** enable OVS NORMAL, STP, `org.onosproject.fwd`, or uncontrolled L2 flooding to make `pingall` succeed.

## Faults and tools

Mandatory faults only: F1 link failure; F2 congestion; F3 ACL/policy error; F4 forwarding loop; F5 missing/incorrect OpenFlow rule. Use s3–s4 for controlled F4. h6 dual-home is optional advanced work, not a sixth required scenario. Do not silently expand scope.

Planned agent tools: `get_topology()`, `ping(src,dst)`, `get_port_status(sw)`, `get_port_stats(sw)`, `get_flow_table(sw)`, `iperf(src,dst)`. M4 is pending until these are a normalised agent-facing interface.

